* TIMES.jl crafted case demo12_bndc (reference/crafted.toml, 14 Nov 2026): bounds on the net
* amount and the production of a commodity at a timeslice above the level the commodity is
* tracked at, which GAMS writes as equations (eqbndcom.mod L16-24: EQ(l)_BNDNET, EQ(l)_BNDPRD)
* and not as bounds of VAR_COMNET and VAR_COMPRD. Added to TIMES_Demo demo12
* (etsap-TIMES/TIMES_Demo @ 962db86, CC BY 4.0), where ELC and the sector electricity
* commodities are tracked at DAYNITE (SD, SN, WD, WN, in the seasons S and W):
* - COM_BNDPRD of ELC at ANNUAL: LO in REG1 2020 (EQG_BNDPRD) and UP in REG1 2030
*   (EQL_BNDPRD), each a sum over the four DAYNITE timeslices; both bind.
* - COM_BNDPRD of ELC at the season S, FX in REG2 2030 (EQE_BNDPRD, a sum over SD and SN).
* - COM_BNDPRD of ELC at WD, UP in REG2 2020: the commodity's own level, so a bound of
*   VAR_COMPRD and no equation.
* - COM_BNDNET of ELC at ANNUAL, LO in REG1 2030 (EQG_BNDNET), and at the season W, UP in
*   REG2 2020 (EQL_BNDNET).
* - COM_BNDNET of ELC at ANNUAL, FX with the value EPS in REG2 2030: EQE_BNDNET with a
*   right-hand side of zero (the FX call has no condition on the value, eqmain.mod L55).
* - COM_BNDNET of RSDELC at ANNUAL, LO with the value EPS in REG1 2020, and of COMELC at
*   ANNUAL, UP with the value INF in REG1 2020: no equation (eqmain.mod L54 and L56: LO NE 0,
*   UP NE INF).
$ONEMPTY
$ONEPS
$ONWARNING
PARAMETER
COM_BNDPRD ' '/
REG1.2020.ELC.ANNUAL.LO 6000
REG1.2030.ELC.ANNUAL.UP 6000
REG2.2030.ELC.S.FX 4100
REG2.2020.ELC.WD.UP 1600
/

PARAMETER
COM_BNDNET ' '/
REG1.2030.ELC.ANNUAL.LO 50
REG2.2020.ELC.W.UP 10
REG2.2030.ELC.ANNUAL.FX EPS
REG1.2020.RSDELC.ANNUAL.LO EPS
REG1.2020.COMELC.ANNUAL.UP INF
/
